 @EntityGraph(attributePaths = "product")
    Optional<ProductImage> findByIdAndDeletedFalse(Long id);

Why Use @EntityGraph?

Without @EntityGraph:

ProductImage image = repository.findByIdAndDeletedFalse(id).get();

Product product = image.getProduct();

This can result in:

SELECT product_image ...

SELECT product ...

(two queries)

With:

@EntityGraph(attributePaths = "product")

Hibernate performs a fetch join and retrieves both entities in a single query, reducing database round trips and preventing the N+1 select problem.